ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.216 g
42.5196850393700814 262.7718897637795408 Td
(3. Retail Buyers & Boutique Owners: Mid-tier commercial buyers who need clear order tracking and specifications without) Tj
T* (cumbersome 20-page legal contracts.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 10.5 Tf
12.0749999999999993 TL
0.153 0.153 0.165 rg
42.5196850393700814 220.5356692913385359 Td
(2.2 Core Commercial Pain Points) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.216 g
42.5196850393700814 203.5277952755905062 Td
(In India, informal commerce accounts for billions of rupees in annual volume. Small suppliers operate on razor-thin margins and) Tj
T* (are uniquely vulnerable to four recurring traps:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.216 g
42.5196850393700814 176.8821259842519567 Td
(1. Unlawful Extended Credit \(The Working Capital Trap\): Large buyers frequently demand 60, 90, or 120 days credit, or stipulate) Tj
T* ("pay-when-paid" terms \(waiting until an overseas export buyer remits funds\). This directly violates Section 15 of the *Micro, Small) Tj
T* (and Medium Enterprises Development Act, 2006* \(MSMED Act\), which mandates a 15-day baseline and caps agreed credit) Tj
T* (terms at an absolute ceiling of 45 days.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.216 g
42.5196850393700814 126.4254330708660063 Td
(2. Arbitrary Debit Notes \(The Post-Delivery Penalty Trap\): Buyers often accept finished garments, hold them for 30 - 60 days,) Tj
T* (and subsequently issue unilateral "debit notes" deducting 20% to 30% of the invoice for alleged loose threads or minor stitching) Tj
T* (defects. Under Section 42 of the *Sale of Goods Act, 1930*, buyers have a duty to examine goods within a reasonable time, after) Tj
T* (which goods are deemed legally accepted.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
9.1999999999999993 TL
0.549 g
490.3981102362204183 22.6771653543306684 Td
